task.statement:
This function builds a frequency table of tags. It works, but it is written the way you would write it in Java — hand-rolled membership check plus init-or-increment branching.

    def count_tags(tags):
        counts = {}
        for tag in tags:
            if tag in counts:
                counts[tag] = counts[tag] + 1
            else:
                counts[tag] = 1
        return counts

